Description: test-fileio: tolerate -EBADF from read_virtual_file(/proc/kcore)
 test_read_virtual_file_one() reads a fixed list of virtual files and, on
 failure, asserts the error is one of an allowed set (privilege errors,
 -ENOENT, -EINVAL, -EFBIG).  In the Athena build container on a 6.12.x
 host kernel, /proc/kcore is masked by the container runtime and the
 read fails with -EBADF, which is not in the set — the assertion aborts
 (SIGABRT) and dh_auto_test fails the whole systemd build:
 .
   read_virtual_file("/proc/kcore", 0): Bad file descriptor
   Assertion 'ERRNO_IS_PRIVILEGE(r) || IN_SET(r, -ENOENT, -EINVAL, -EFBIG)'
   failed at src/test/test-fileio.c:1023
 .
 The July 2026 amd64 world build passed on an older host kernel, where
 the masked read surfaced as a privilege error instead; the behaviour is
 host-kernel-dependent, not a systemd regression.  Add -EBADF to the
 allowed set for exactly this masked-/proc/kcore case.
Origin: vendor, Athena-Build
Forwarded: not-needed (test-environment tolerance; Debian 252.x specific)
Author: Athena-Build
Last-Update: 2026-11-08
---
--- a/src/test/test-fileio.c
+++ b/src/test/test-fileio.c
@@ -1024,7 +1024,8 @@
                                   IN_SET(r,
                                          -ENOENT,  /* Some of the files might be absent */
                                          -EINVAL,  /* too small reads from /proc/self/pagemap trigger EINVAL */
-                                         -EFBIG)); /* /proc/kcore and /proc/self/pagemap should be too large */
+                                         -EFBIG,   /* /proc/kcore and /proc/self/pagemap should be too large */
+                                         -EBADF)); /* /proc/kcore: masked by the container runtime; read fails EBADF on newer kernels */
                 } else
                         log_info("read_virtual_file(\"%s\", %zu): %s (%zu bytes)", filename, max_size, r ? "non-truncated" : "truncated", size);
         }
